-- title:
--   Degeneracy map q↦ q^ℓ sends the place of τ to that of ℓτ
-- statement:
--   Fix positive integers $N$ and $\ell$. For a level $M$, write $\mathbb{C}F_M$ for [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange ℂ (ModularCurve.modularFunctionFieldFull M)`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), the intermediate field of $\mathbb{C}((q))$ generated over $\mathbb{C}$ by the coefficientwise images of the $\mathbb{Q}$-field generated by the divisor expansions of level $M$, and let $\beta=$ [`ModularCurve.heckeBetaBar ℂ N ℓ`](def/ModularCurve_HeckeOperator.html#L98) $:\mathbb{C}F_N\to\mathbb{C}F_{N\ell}$ be the $\mathbb{C}$-algebra map induced by the substitution $q\mapsto q^{\ell}$ on Laurent series (reindexing exponents by multiplication by $\ell$). Let $D$, resp. $D'$, be a complex place dictionary of level $N$, resp. $N\ell$: an assignment $\tau\mapsto$ `pt` $\tau$ of places of $\mathbb{C}F_M$ over $\mathbb{C}$ (valuation subrings containing $\mathbb{C}$, proper, with principal ideals), invariant under $\Gamma_0(M)$, together with positive integers `ramification` $\tau$, such that $x$ lies in the valuation subring of `pt` $\tau$ exactly when $\|\,$`realize` $M\,x\,\|$ is bounded near $\tau$ on a punctured neighbourhood, and such that the meromorphic order of $z\mapsto$ `realize` $M\,x$ at $\tau$ equals `ramification` $\tau$ times $\operatorname{ord}_{\mathrm{pt}\,\tau}(x)$ for $x\neq 0$. Assume $\beta$ is integral, and let $\tau\in\mathfrak{H}$. Then, first, the pullback $\beta^{-1}$ of the valuation subring of $D'.\mathrm{pt}\,\tau$ is the place $D.\mathrm{pt}$ of the point [`ModularForm.heckeDiagMatrix`](def/ModularForm_HeckeOperator.html#L21) $\ell\cdot\tau$, i.e. of $\ell\tau$ (the action of $\begin{pmatrix}\ell&0\\0&1\end{pmatrix}\in\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{R})$); and second, $D'.\mathrm{ramification}\,\tau$ times the ramification index of $D'.\mathrm{pt}\,\tau$ along $\beta$ — the least positive value of $\operatorname{ord}_{D'.\mathrm{pt}\,\tau}(\beta f)$ over nonzero $f\in\mathbb{C}F_N$ — equals $D.\mathrm{ramification}$ at $\ell\tau$.
--
--   This is the analytic description of the second degeneracy map $X_0(N\ell)\to X_0(N)$, given on $q$-expansions by $q\mapsto q^{\ell}$ and on the upper half plane by $z\mapsto \ell z$, together with the resulting comparison of local ramification data at $\tau$ and $\ell\tau$. It is used in the computation of the pullback of a point divisor, [`ModularCurve.ComplexPlaceDictionary.heckeDivBar_single_pt`](thm.html#ModularCurve.ComplexPlaceDictionary.heckeDivBar_single_pt), in the construction of the Hecke correspondence on $X_0(N)$.
-- source:
